    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.deps\n\n### Description\n\nI'm not sure how widespread this is in the general plugin ecosystem, but I'm aware of https://gitlab.com/HiPhish/rainbow-delimiters.nvim giving me headaches due to them having submodules with strictly testing-related dependencies that can change unpredictably and mess with automated plugin-manager git checkouts.\n\nI'd like there to be a switch in the plugin specification that disables submodules to avoid that, e.g. `submodules = false`",
