    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\n> ... but I'm aware of https://gitlab.com/HiPhish/rainbow-delimiters.nvim giving me headaches due to them having submodules with strictly testing-related dependencies that can change unpredictably and mess with automated plugin-manager git checkouts.\n\nCan you please elaborate on this?\n\nIn my mind, if plugin decided it needs to have submodules, then they need to be present. If they are only for testing, then I'd say it is not the best practice from the plugin to include them. And it looks like [it was the case here also](https://gitlab.com/HiPhish/rainbow-delimiters.nvim/-/blob/master/.gitmodules?ref_type=heads#L1) prior to \"move to `vim.pack`\" commit about two months ago.",
